No source code from that project is included here. The following parts of
WikiLM were written independently against its published design, and each
credits it in a comment at the point of use:

  - src/retrieval.ts, src/askCheck.ts — the seed-selection cascade (lexical,
    keyword, graph expansion), the title-over-body scoring weight, and
    answering from general knowledge with a label rather than refusing.

  - src/vaultLint.ts — the vault scanners: orphans, dead links, empty pages,
    missing aliases.

  - src/vaultFix.ts, src/modals.ts — dead-link repair by tiered name
    resolution, and a lint report whose fix buttons are gated on counts.

  - src/topicNote.ts, src/suggestPlan.ts — filing new material into a section
    of an existing page, and creating that section when it is absent.

WikiLM's own policies differ from upstream's where they conflict: notably,
new material is appended into an existing page whenever one is related,
rather than given a page of its own unless an existing page denotes the same
thing.
